# P59X: session-artifact patterns, not instances -- P60-LEDGER.md and the two
# P59-C*.csv extracts (untracked by this same pass) are the first instances this
# repo ever tracked of these shapes; the rules below exist so a future P61+ ledger
# or extract never gets tracked again by default. Root-anchored (leading /) on
# purpose -- these are repository-root session artifacts specifically, not a
# pattern meant to reach into db/fixtures/ or anywhere else a real, load-bearing
# CSV or markdown file might legitimately live.
/P*-LEDGER.md
/P*-*.csv

# P59X: the two internal-strategy/business-plan documents, exact filenames only.
# Deliberately NOT a broader text/* rule -- text/LedgeX_Engineering_Reference_
# Spec_v1_46.txt and text/LedgeX_Implementation_Rules_v1_4.txt are the spec
# SOURCE (docs/LEDGEX_SPEC.md and docs/LEDGEX_RULES.md are generated from them,
# build/ledgex_source.py) and must stay tracked; text/LedgeX_San_Jose_Data_
# Source_Checklist_v1_2.txt is also unaffected. A wildcard here would silently
# break `make docs`/`make qa` the next time either spec file changed.
/text/LedgeX_Municipal_Data_and_API_Audit_Internal_Strategy_v1_1.txt
/text/LedgeX_Vision_and_Early_Stage_Business_Plan_2_1_4.txt

# P59X: one stray root-level prompt file, untracked by this pass.
/tier-redefinition-prompt.txt

# NOTE, not a rule: the LEDGEX-*.txt prompt corpus at the repository root (and
# LEDGEX-*.md handoff/report files alongside it) has never been tracked, by
# convention, since before this repository's history begins -- no .gitignore
# entry covers it because none has ever been needed. This comment exists so a
# future reader does not mistake "no rule" for "not yet gitignored" and add one
# that would make an already-untracked convention look newly enforced.
